# Kept out of the `git archive` snapshot the editor bundles as its sample
# project (the editor's `bundleDemo` Gradle task).
#
# Both files name every planted issue and its fix. The sample exists to show
# the project tools FINDING those issues — project_health, validate_project,
# check_links, conref_audit — and an agent pointed at the project will open a
# root-level file called ISSUES.md, which is competent behaviour rather than
# cheating. Shipping the answer key alongside the puzzle meant the demo could
# not demonstrate the one thing it is for.
#
# They stay here, in the repo, where maintainers and the editor's e2e workflow
# use them: e2e checks out this repository, not the bundled zip.
#
# The walkthrough for users lives in the documentation:
# https://dogsbay.ai/dogsbay-xml-docs/getting-started/tutorial-agentic
ISSUES.md export-ignore
DEMO.md export-ignore
